{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-03T09:44:32.398Z","data":{"text":"Done. Task 12 is complete.\n\nSummary of changes:\n- **`src/cli/run.ts`**: `runCli` now uses `processStderr`/`processStdout` (with explicit `\\n`) instead of `console.*`, preserving bytes, streams and exit codes.\n- **`src/cli/index.ts`**: the `lint` action passes `options` directly to `lintCommand`, dropping its own `stdout` writer.\n- **`tests/cli-config-errors.test.ts`**: captures through `runCliCaptured` instead of overriding `console.error`, asserting the same stderr line/text and exit code.\n- **`tests/cli-no-direct-output.test.ts`** (new): scans every `.ts` under `src/cli/` for `console.`, `process.stdout.write`, `process.stderr.write` (comments stripped, `command-inputs.ts` exempt), and holds the typed `CommandInputs` table with a missing-name check for exported `*Command` functions.\n\nNotable deviation (documented in the result): `browserCommand` in `serve.ts` is a synchronous helper ending in `Command` and lies outside scope, so the table includes a wrapper for it that ignores inputs; real commands pass `CommandInputs` so the typecheck still guards them.\n\nVerification:\n- Task verify: `node --import tsx --import ./tests/git-test-env.ts --test tests/cli-no-direct-output.test.ts` — 6 pass.\n- Proposal verify: `pnpm verify` — typechecks, build, all tests, lint pass.\n\n`Touched: src/cli/run.ts, src/cli/index.ts, tests/cli-config-errors.test.ts, tests/cli-no-direct-output.test.ts`"}}
